 Ferns, and is much more effectual than they, both for inward and outward griefs, and is accounted singularly good in wounds, bruises, or the like. The decoction to be drank, or boiled into an ointment of oil, as a balsam or balm, and so it is singularly good against bruises, and bones broken, or out of joint, and gives much ease to the cholic and splenetic diseases: as also for ruptures or burstings. The decoction of the root in white wine, provokes urine exceedingly, and cleanses the bladder and passages of urine.","spans":[{"start":189,"end":195,"concept_id":"wounds","polarity":"therapeutic"},{"start":197,"end":204,"concept_id":"bruises","polarity":"therapeutic"},{"start":339,"end":346,"concept_id":"bruises","polarity":"therapeutic"},{"start":369,"end":381,"concept_id":"bruises","polarity":"therapeutic"},{"start":410,"end":416,"concept_id":"colic","polarity":"therapeutic"},{"start":421,"end":430,"concept_id":"spleen_disease","polarity":"therapeutic"},{"start":517,"end":531,"concept_id":"diuresis","polarity":"action"},{"start":562,"end":569,"concept_id":"kidney_disease","polarity":"therapeutic"}]}},"gloss":{"cul:119-osmond-royal-or-water-fern":{"189":"wounds (green, fresh, inward, old); wound-herb","197":"bruises","339":"bruises","369":"members out of joint (dislocation)","410":"cholic: colic, griping abdominal pain","421":"splenetic: suffering from the spleen","517":"provokes urine: diuretic","562":"bladder"}},"images":[]}